      "description": "Watch Bournemouth vs Everton highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. The Premier League encounter between Bournemouth and Everton proved to be a gripping tactical battle where momentum shifted with every passing phase. Both sides displayed immense physical commitment, ensuring that the outcome remained uncertain until the final moments of play. Scott Finds the Breakthrough On August 29, 2026, the match opened with both teams struggling to find their rhythm amidst a flurry of early corners and goal kicks. However, the deadlock was finally broken in the 41st minute. Following a key pass from Rayan , Evanilson provided the assist for Alex Scott , whose right-footed shot took a deflection before finding the back of the net. The goal gave Bournemouth a well-deserved lead heading into the break, rewarding their superior ball possession and patience in the final third. VAR Controversy and Sustained Pressure Everton emerged for the second half with renewed intent, pushing higher up the pitch to unsettle the hosts. The game reached a boiling point in the 55th minute when a VAR check for a potential Everton penalty halted play. To the frustration of the visiting fans, the referee decided to stick with the original call, denying the Toffees a chance from the spot. As the clock ticked down, both managers turned to their benches, with Bournemouth introducing Tyler Adams and Everton bringing on Beto to inject more physicality into the contest. Tarkowski Strikes Late to Deny the Cherries Just as Bournemouth seemed destined to secure all three points, the narrative took a dramatic turn in stoppage time. In the 91st minute, James Tarkowski showcased his predatory instincts by finding the net with a precise right-footed finish to level the score at 1-1. The closing stages were frantic, marked by a tactical foul from Carlos Alcaraz that earned him a yellow card as he stopped a dangerous counter-attack. Despite late efforts from both sides, the referee’s final whistle confirmed a hard-fought draw in a match defined by late drama."
