      "description": "Watch Preston North End vs Everton highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 26, 2026. The Carabao Cup journey continued as Preston North End hosted Everton on August 26, 2026. Fans gathered at the stadium expecting a competitive knockout encounter between the two historic clubs. Everton Break the Deadlock The match began with both sides testing each other's resolve, but it was Everton who struck the first blow. In the 25th minute, Vitaliy Mykolenko displayed excellent vision to find Thierno Barry with a precise assist. Barry made no mistake, finishing clinically to give the visitors the lead. Preston North End attempted to rally before the break, but the Toffees' backline remained organized, ensuring they headed into halftime with their advantage intact. The Thierno Barry Show The second half saw Everton shift into a higher gear, led by a sensational performance from Thierno Barry . In the 59th minute, Barry found the back of the net once again to double the lead. Preston manager responded with a flurry of substitutions, bringing on the likes of Harry Clarke and Alfie Devine to spark a comeback, but the momentum remained firmly with the Premier League side. The game was effectively put to rest during a devastating two-minute spell. In the 71st minute, Brennan Johnson set up Thierno Barry for his hat-trick. Just sixty seconds later, the duo combined again as Barry turned provider for Brennan Johnson to fire home the fourth goal. As the clock wound down, Everton introduced fresh legs including Carlos Alcaraz and Tyrique George , comfortably seeing out the final whistle to progress in the competition."
